ou're a fool if I ever met one. That was a      quicksand bog, of course. And now you are sinking, sinking, sinking.    Happy journey, or to put it another way:                                Ho,ho! Bathing in oil! Your clothes are saturated, and your skin is     pretty slippery. You should try wrestling. Beware of fire!              Now that's nice! Cleopatra used some kind of milk, but you really take  the price! Vintage port! Really!! Your clothes are rather wet, and your face not specially cleaner.                                             YYEEEEOOWW!! Scalding! Your skin is very hot and red, and your clothes  are beyind description (what's left of them, that is!!)                 Seems you got rid of them. Sentry dwarfs surely has to return to their  posts so no other adventurer may sneak past.                            Now you're in the frying pan!!                                          Did you really think sentry dwarfs let you pass them by? You were       thrown back by a lance so hard you just about lost your breath!         There's a hot pursuit behind you. You'd better try to fend them off!    The guards are taken a little aback by your sudden attack. You manage   to hit one of them a good blow before they are quite ready for the      fight. Go to it, man!!                                                  Lances are lowered! You're under attack! You are hit in the leg by a    lance!                                                                  You are attacked by a sentry dwarf. He gives a mighty blow with his     big baaaad axe.                                                         He just misses with his deadly stroke, but nicks you in the arm!        He cleaves you from head to toe! ....You know there's much inside you?  With one of them out of the way for the moment, you manage to fight the other one reasonably well. You're hard-pressed, but manage to give him  a nasty wound in the leg.                                               With you pressing the attack, the first sentry, altough having recover- ed, is seriously hurt once more. He goes down heavily, being out of the fight for the moment.                                                   The one with the wound in the leg is back in the fight. As you are now  taking advantage of his weakened state, you once more get in a good     blow, knocking him off his feet and having him at your mercy.           That's it! As you give him the finishing touch, he flashes brightly and disappears. However, the first dwarf have managed to regain his feet,   and stabs at you with his lance.                                        Altough he's weak, he's a sturdy fellow! The lance went right through   you, and that does you in.                                              He's rather feeble, however, and you manage to push the lance aside.    And that was the end of the first dwarf, who likewise disappears.       Your puny gestures avail you nothing. A big bad axe cleanly snitches    off your head.                                                          Even as you attack one of the sentries, the other one manage to get in  a wellaimed blow at you. I'm afraid he aimed too well.                  I'm afraid you're in a bad way. They advance on you with lances at the  ready. You had better do something real quick!!                         You have to fight them to survive, you know. Now you're done for, as    you are quite helpless with your bad leg. Sorry about that!             Even if you don't fight, you had a lucky escape this time.              You didn't really think they would let you pass the second time? Now    you're badly hurt, and unable to do anything to defend yourself.        Well, oh, well. My oh my. You're in the precence of the Mountain King.  Can you imagine a BIG dwarf? Or perhaps rather a fair-looking troll?    That's what's on the throne right before you. He casts a suspicious     look at you as you enter, appearently taken by surprise that you have   passed the guards.                                                      The King takes your bottle with obvious delight, and sets it to his     mouth. After tasting, he gives a big grin. Yelling something funny, he  invites you to partake in his hoard of beer. Several smallish dwarves   appear with tankards and bottles of all kinds.                          As you have nothing to offer, the Mountain King grows rather grumpy     very soon. He yells for some underlings to take care of the idiot,                                                                                                                                                                                                                              Very well. Let's see .... ah - yes, here we are. As I am a most         sensitive computer, I must leave you now. Hope to see you soon -        eh - sorry. Happy journey ! (Not pretty likely, huh?) Well, good luck!! Then he eyes your bottle with a I-don't-believe-my-eyes look.           The Mountain King gives a delighted shout, saying that was a jolly      good song.                                                              The Mountain King claps his big hand on his throne, shouting that this  was exactly the right song for this occasion. Thereafter he slips       down from the throne and goes into a heavy sleep beside it. A loud      snoring soon fills the room.                                            The Mountain King grins with delight as he sees you guzzling the        amber fluid. He insists on you drinking some more.                      The Mountain King eyes you with a speculative gaze.                     The Mountain King eyes you with an irritated glance, and asks you why   the HELL you are still hanging around here. He waves his hand,          The Mountain King is still snoring. The room is now empty of everything,else (except the statues, throne and table). As you enter, the King     opens his eyes for a moment, yells something, goes to sleep, and        Silly thing. You're not allowed to take that, you moron. The Mountain   King snorts derisively, gives a small gesture,                          There's no Mountain King around here!!                                  The Mountain King declines your offer.                                  several small windows pops open in the walls. There also pops out a     number of arrows, which unfortunately all have you as their target.     whereupon some more guards appear. They strip you of your valuables,    and takes you with them. You are allowed the choice between roasting in the lava river or boiling in the cooking river. Which one is it to be?  It's cold, but OK.                                                      OUCH!!!                                                                 There's no wall to kick here.                                           I will not!!                                                            Oh, so you are one of those, are you??                                  You already have a ring on your finger.                                 There's no circlet here.                                                You don't wear a circlet.                                               Extremely sorry, but that I cannot do yet.                              Your axe bounces harmlessly off the shield of the guard.                Your axe hits a guard and gives him a nasty wound in the thigh.         Very well.                                                              HOO-HAW!!                                                               W[[[[[[[[[[[[[[[[[[[[                                                   Before we continue, I'd like to call you a bastard!! Let's go!!         You are still at the same place, and with company!                      